  "definition": "A vegetation index is a mathematical combination of spectral reflectances designed to emphasise vegetation-related contrast. The sensor first measures radiance. Calibration, atmospheric correction and, for some products, correction for viewing and illumination geometry produce the reflectances used in the index. The index is therefore a derived spectral quantity rather than a direct measurement of plant health, biomass or productivity.[^1][^2]",
